["Pulsing Heart Beat Light", "glow", 55, 3, "battery holder (2×AA),AA batteries,LED (3V),crocodile clip leads,mini switch,paper,thin card,paint", "! A grown-up fits the batteries and checks every clip.|Cut a heart from thin card and paint it red.|Mount an LED behind the heart so the light shines through.|! A grown-up wires the LED and switch to the battery pack.|Press the switch rhythmically like a heartbeat and watch the heart pulse.", "A switch controls when current flows to a light.", "Make a night-light that pulses once a second.", "t"],
["Foil Maze Buzzer Game", "squish", 60, 3, "battery holder (2×AA),AA batteries,buzzer (3V),crocodile clip leads,aluminium foil,cardboard box,paper clips,thin card", "Cut a winding path from foil strips on a card base, leaving a thin gap beside each wall.|Make a wand from a paper clip bent into a loop.|! A grown-up wires the foil walls, the wand and the buzzer in a circuit.|Trace the path with the wand without touching the walls.|Time yourself and count how many times the buzzer sounds.", "Touching the wall completes the circuit and the buzzer sounds.", "Make a harder maze with a smaller gap.", "t"],
["Electric Quiz Board", "glow", 65, 3, "battery holder (2×AA),AA batteries,LED (3V),crocodile clip leads,aluminium foil,paper clips,cardboard box,thin card", "Write six questions on a card with six possible answers down the side.|Fix a paper clip beside each question and each answer.|! A grown-up wires each correct pair to the LED with foil strips behind the card.|Touch the two ends of a wire lead to the clips and watch for the light.|Swap the cards around to make a new quiz.", "A circuit is only complete when the two matching clips connect.", "Make a quiz about the solar system.", "t"],
["Dark-Sensing Night-light Teddy", "nightbot", 75, 3, "solar garden light,cardboard box,fabric scraps,thin card,paint,googly eyes,masking tape", "! A grown-up opens an old solar light and keeps the sensor and LED in the housing.|Build a teddy-shaped box from card and fabric scraps.|Place the sensor on the head so it sees the room, with the LED in the belly.|Switch off the room light and watch the teddy glow.|Test in daylight and note the difference.", "Light sensors can turn a night-light on automatically.", "Make a nightlight that turns off when it hears a clap.", "t"],
["Rolling Marble Light Switch", "tilt", 65, 3, "battery holder (2×AA),AA batteries,LED (3V),crocodile clip leads,aluminium foil,marbles,cardboard box,thin card", "! A grown-up keeps marbles away from little ones.|Make a card track with foil along the bottom.|! A grown-up wires the end of the track to an LED.|Roll the marble down and watch the LED light as it closes the circuit.|Tilt the box to make the marble roll back and the light go out.", "A rolling marble can work as a moving switch.", "Make a light that comes on only when the box is tipped left.", "t"],
["Bike Bell Reflector Model", "bump", 70, 2, "cardboard box,thin card,aluminium foil,bottle caps,paint,string,paper plates", "Build a toy bike from card with paper-plate wheels.|Add foil reflectors to the wheels and back.|Shine a torch at it in a dark room and see how the light bounces back.|Test reflectors in different shapes and sizes.|Write a safety rule about being seen on a bike.", "Reflectors send light back towards its source so riders are seen.", "Design a reflector that works from all angles.", "t"],
["Treasure Chest Lock Alarm", "squish", 75, 3, "battery holder (2×AA),AA batteries,buzzer (3V),crocodile clip leads,aluminium foil,paper clips,cardboard box,paint,clothes pegs", "Decorate a small box as a treasure chest.|Fix foil under the lid and on the rim so lifting it breaks the contact.|! A grown-up wires the contacts through a buzzer and battery.|Close the lid and set the alarm.|Open it and listen for the sound.", "Opening the lid changes the switch and sets off the alarm.", "Hide a second switch to catch sneaky guards.", "t"]
